│ the next chunk                                                               │
│       of sorted characters of the same length, but with characters in        │
│ descending order.                                                            │
│     - Spaces and their positions are preserved.                              │
│     - Return type must be int, so we return the ASCII sum of the output      │
│ string.                                                                      │
│                                                                              │
│     Example:                                                                 │
│     s = "Hello World!!!"                                                     │
│     Sorted all chars ascending: ['!', '!', '!', ' ', 'H', 'W', 'd', 'e',     │
│ 'l', 'l', 'l', 'o', 'o', 'r']                                                │
│     Words in s: "Hello" (5 chars), "World!!!" (8 chars including             │
│ punctuation)                                                                 │
│     Actually, "World!!!" is 8 chars? No, "World!!!" is 8 chars: W o r l d !  │
│ ! !                                                                          │
│     Spaces preserved in position.                                            │
│                                                                              │
│     So words: ["Hello", "World!!!"]                                          │
│     Take first 5 chars from sorted: ['!', '!', '!', ' ', 'H'] -> but space   │
│ is not part of word, so we skip spaces in assignment                         │
│     Actually, we must only assign sorted letters to words (letters are       │
│ non-space chars), spaces remain as is.                                       │
│                                                                              │
│     So total non-space chars = total letters + punctuation in words.         │
│     Let's do:                                                                │
│     - Extract all non-space chars, sort ascending.                           │
│     - For each word in s (separated by spaces), take next chunk of sorted    │
│ chars length len(word),                                                      │
│       sort that chunk descending, and place it.                              │
│     - Spaces remain at same positions.                                       │
│                                                                              │
│     Finally, join all words and spaces to form output string.                │
│                                                                              │
│     Return ASCII sum (int) of output string.                                 │
│                                                                              │
│     This matches examples:                                                   │
│     anti_shuffle('Hi') returns 'iH' but also 'Hi'  -> sorted letters         │
│ ascending: 'Hi' -> 'Hi', descending for word: 'iH'                           │
│     anti_shuffle('hello') returns 'olleh' but also 'ehllo' -> sorted         │
